    en: "This paper form is from 2019 and still uses the advance purposes and paragraph numbers (68B, 68J, 68K...) of the old EPF Scheme, 1952. Since then EPFO's Central Board (13 October 2025) decided to merge the 13 advance purposes into 3 categories, keep 25% of contributions as a minimum balance, and change the waiting time after leaving a job to 12 months for PF and 36 months for pension withdrawal. The Government has also notified the EPF Scheme, 2026 (G.S.R. 525(E), 29 June 2026). The new scheme replaces (supersedes) the EPF Scheme, 1952, so the paragraph numbers on this form are from the old scheme and the form may not match the new rules. Most members now file this claim online on the EPFO Member Portal or UMANG with Aadhaar OTP. Before you submit the paper form, ask your EPFO office whether they still accept it and which rules apply.",
